{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/808314-do-vampires-frenzy-when-they-meet-each-other","id":808314,"title":"Do vampires frenzy when they meet each other?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-13T16:50:53-08:00","id":808314,"title":"Do vampires frenzy when they meet each other?","content":"Someone told me that when 2 vampires meet they have to roll to resist frenzy. I'm combing through my copy of 2nd edition, and I'm not seeing that anywhere. Is it something from 1st that didn't carry over or what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T16:55:51-08:00","id":808316,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's a first edition only thing I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T16:57:32-08:00","id":808318,"title":"","content":"Oh good. That sounds massively stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T16:58:51-08:00","id":808319,"title":"","content":"This was a thing in 1st edition called Predator's Taint. The first time two vampires met, the one with higher Blood Potency would have to roll to resist Frenzy with the goal of feeding on the other, and the one with lower Blood Potency would have to roll to resist Frenzying with the intention to flee. I'm 2nd edition, the Predator's Taint was replaced with the Predatory Aura and Lashing Out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T17:03:17-08:00","id":808322,"title":"","content":"Why was that ever a thing? That sounds disastrous. How would elysium ever function?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T17:10:00-08:00","id":808323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neckbeard the Pirate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/808314-do-vampires-frenzy-when-they-meet-each-other?p=808322#post808322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why was that ever a thing? That sounds disastrous. How would elysium ever function?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, most of the vampires that attend Elysium have already met before. It only happened the first time they met. But yeah, it was disastrous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T17:10:34-08:00","id":808324,"title":"","content":"Leaving that behind is one of the best things 2e did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T18:01:51-08:00","id":808349,"title":"","content":"A lot of aspects of first edition's 'big three' seem like they were put in solely to distance themselves from the previous edition. Second edition has really gone a long way towards making them more of their own games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T19:40:35-08:00","id":808395,"title":"","content":"Predator's Taint was there to create a sense of isolation and an edge to Kindred society - it's one of a few design decisions made, in part, to keep the neofeudal structure very small scale and very local. I think they talk a little bit about it in Damnation City; Predator's Taint, as well as setting assumptions like &quot;vampire's don't really use communication technology&quot; and talking up travel between cities like it was a death sentence, created this neon sign that said &quot;OUTSIDERS NOT WELCOME!&quot;<br /> <br /> While I think it was certainly an interesting decision and isn't <i>necessarily</i> bad on it's own, I feel that although it existed to drive Requiem from the global-spanning vast machinations of undead society that permeated Masquerade, the fact that a lot of <i>other</i> design decisions (covenant structure, domain hierarchy, etc.) <i>played up</i> similarities with Masquerade that Predator's Taint stood directly at odds with meant that it was a bitter, disjointed feeling every time it came up.<br /> <br /> If the game had been more about small numbers of rival coteries staking out territory - kinda like Werewolf, now that I think about it - then maybe Predator's Taint would have been -great-. As it was included in a game where the drama lay within the social dynamics, it clashed incredibly hard.<br /> <br /> Edit: Now with 2e, Predator's Aura can add all the edge that the ST wants without risking derailing every new encounter. Best of both worlds!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 01-13-2016, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T09:35:23-08:00","id":808768,"title":"","content":"It should also be said, while there are no hard rules for it anymore, it still is a thing in the fiction (see pg. 72, VtR 2e). The ST can still make use of the concept by calling for Frenzy checks when dramatically appropriate, especially in the aforementioned high stakes situations or when two vampires meet under inauspicious circumstances (like an unknown intruder in your territory).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:45:39-08:00","id":808833,"title":"","content":"Or when somebody has just used the Predatory Aura on you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:01:59-08:00","id":808917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neckbeard the Pirate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/808314-do-vampires-frenzy-when-they-meet-each-other?p=808322#post808322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why was that ever a thing? That sounds disastrous. How would elysium ever function?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Predator's Taint was also ST discretion when it came into play. Going to court would put you on edge but no need to really roll. Finding a Vampire you don't know standing over a corpse at the entrance to your haven ten minutes before dawn WAS cause for a check. I'm glad to see it go too if only because of how much division it formented. I think it mostly got a bad rap from over-zealous ST's asking for frenzy checks nonstop instead of at dramatically appropriate moments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:39:30-08:00","id":808959,"title":"","content":"There were also a fair number of easily accessible powers that mitigated Predator's Taint. Obfuscate 1 made it so you didn't trigger other vampires (though you still had to roll yourself), and Protean 1 made it so higher BP vampires always rolled as though your Blood Potency was equal to theirs. I can count the number of Frenzy checks that were <i>actually</i> rolled due to Predator's Taint in my 4 years of LARPing in college on two hands and the number of times a character failed the roll on one.<br /> <br /> That's the main reason I'm glad they did away with it. Most people I've played with either ignored it, or used it so sparingly that it only came up at moments where it would have been dramatically appropriate even without the rule. It was mostly just wasted wordcount in the core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-14-2016, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T18:00:58-08:00","id":809267,"title":"","content":"You're overreacting a little. It wasn't meant to roll everytime Kindred met with each other for the first time. Nickpre84 is right - that was absolutely under ST discretion and we always saw it like sixth sense in Highlander, when they felt presence of other immortals through unpleasant sensation. Situation requiring you to roll should really be rare and uncommon - that kind of situation when your Beast response with &quot;fight or flight&quot; should really be the wisest and most appropriate.<br /> <br /> It is the fault of Storytellers who put too much emphasis on RAW over RAI that lead to abusing this rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10834-mictlantecuhtli","name":"Mictlantecuhtli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T18:41:33-08:00","id":809286,"title":"","content":"This wasn't so much a mechanical problem as just a slight problem with how the information was presented in the book. Under the &quot;System&quot; section the rule was described as applying whenever Vampires meet for the first time. It then describes the mechanics in precise detail. Then a couple of paragraphs later, flowing over the jump between two pages in a fluff based section called &quot;Storytelling the Predator's Taint&quot; it then contradicts how it works and states that it doesn't apply all the time. This was exceptionally confusing, since most people don't read the book cover to cover. You just look up something you want to know about, like predator's taint, read the system and get back to playing the game. Especially for long-term players of VTM who often assumed that they understood the basics already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T01:29:16-08:00","id":809438,"title":"","content":"I straight up didn't remember that was the case, and I might have missed it if I were rereading the book before running it. As Michael says, it's a matter of presentation - it's not the first mechanics that was slightly but significantly misremembered to the point of twisting it around completely. Like I said, I prefer that 2e goes with an easier Predator's Aura that can be cranked up instead of the Taint that can be cranked down, for this reason.<br /> <br /> Also, I was talking with someone about Predator's Taint and he genuinely liked the mechanic. On top of adding that edge and isolation I talked about earlier, he thought it was neat that the Taint forced Kindred to evaluate how they interact, often keeping neonates in seclusion and introducing them in smaller, controlled environments as well as giving them time and focus to meditate, allowing the fledglings to gather themselves and put their best foot forward. In fact, I wouldn't be surprised if the person I was talking to would have preferred that the Taint lingered in a much more muted version after the first encounter, though he didn't say so. Food for thought!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T06:59:34-08:00","id":809556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/808314-do-vampires-frenzy-when-they-meet-each-other?p=809438#post809438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I straight up didn't remember that was the case, and I might have missed it if I were rereading the book before running it. As Michael says, it's a matter of presentation - it's not the first mechanics that was slightly but significantly misremembered to the point of twisting it around completely. Like I said, I prefer that 2e goes with an easier Predator's Aura that can be cranked up instead of the Taint that can be cranked down, for this reason.<br /> <br /> Also, I was talking with someone about Predator's Taint and he genuinely liked the mechanic. On top of adding that edge and isolation I talked about earlier, he thought it was neat that the Taint forced Kindred to evaluate how they interact, often keeping neonates in seclusion and introducing them in smaller, controlled environments as well as giving them time and focus to meditate, allowing the fledglings to gather themselves and put their best foot forward. In fact, I wouldn't be surprised if the person I was talking to would have preferred that the Taint lingered in a much more muted version after the first encounter, though he didn't say so. Food for thought!</div> </div> </div> </div>It was also predicated in unexpected meetings and not in areas like Elyseum where you you knew you were going to meet fellow kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}